Package: deconflate
Type: Package
Title: Comorbidity Adjustment of Disease Impact Estimates
Version: 0.3.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Philip", "Rasmussen", email = "phr@sund.ku.dk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Adjusts ("de-conflates") single-disease impact estimates for
    statistical associations between diseases, so that impacts can be
    aggregated without double counting. Implements the published proportional
    approximation of Rasmussen et al. (2022) <doi:10.1016/j.prevetmed.2022.105617>,
    an exact simultaneous solution of the underlying additive impact
    equations for crude estimates and for coefficients of additive regressions
    with recorded adjustment sets, and a global model that fits a
    maximum-entropy distribution of disease combinations by iterative
    proportional fitting and incorporates specified pairwise impact
    interactions and three-way association scenarios. Hazard ratios are
    adjusted with a separate multiplicative adapter, with attributable risk.
    Includes Shapley attribution, feasibility checks, Monte Carlo propagation
    of input uncertainty with stability diagnostics, Latin hypercube and
    importance sampling, sensitivity screening and reproduction of the
    published analyses.
